PROPRIETARY LICENCE — ALL RIGHTS RESERVED
Repository: zehair-louzza/Blueseatra
Version 2.0, 10 October 2026

Copyright © 2025-2026 Zehair Louzza, trading as "Blueseatra", Paris, France.
All rights reserved.

1. Owner and scope. The rights holder is Zehair Louzza, trading as
   "Blueseatra" (the "Owner"). This licence covers all content of the
   zehair-louzza/Blueseatra repository and its history (the "Software"):
   - source and object code, scripts, migrations and configuration;
   - documentation, diagrams, screenshots, texts, prompts and AI templates;
   - the "Blueseatra" name, logo and other distinctive signs;
   - databases, normalised catalogues, test sets and measurements, which are
     also protected by the database right (French IP Code, art. L.341-1 ff.).

2. No licence granted. No right to use, copy, display, modify, adapt,
   translate, distribute or commercialise the Software is granted without the
   Owner's prior, written and signed permission.
   - Publishing on GitHub is neither a licence nor a waiver. The only right
     granted to third parties is the one GitHub's Terms of Service require for
     public repositories: viewing the repository and forking it on GitHub.
     That right allows no other use of a copy, in particular no execution, no
     modification and no distribution outside GitHub.
   - In particular, the following are prohibited: copying; running, installing
     or deploying the Software, even for trial, internal or free use;
     modifying it or creating derivative works; providing it or any of its
     functions to third parties, including as SaaS, API, resale, rental or
     sublicence; building a competing product from it; extracting a
     substantial part of its databases and catalogues; removing proprietary
     notices; circumventing technical protection measures.

3. AI and text and data mining. The Owner expressly reserves its rights
   against text and data mining (French IP Code, art. L.122-5-3 III; Article 4
   of Directive (EU) 2019/790). Using the Software to train, fine-tune,
   evaluate or feed any AI model, search system or dataset is prohibited
   without written permission. This reservation applies subject only to the rights that
   GitHub's Terms of Service grant to GitHub, Inc. to host and operate the
   service on which the repository is published.

4. Statutory exceptions. Mandatory exceptions under French law (IP Code,
   art. L.122-5, L.122-6-1 and L.342-3) remain available to lawful users,
   within their strict conditions.

5. Third parties. Third-party components remain under their own licences.
   Distributor and manufacturer brands, designations, references and prices
   belong to their respective owners; no right in them is granted.

6. Contributions. Any contribution is accepted only if its author assigns to
   the Owner, free of charge and exclusively, worldwide, for the full legal
   term and for all modes of exploitation, the economic rights in it. The
   author warrants that they are entitled to make this assignment.

7. Confidentiality and security. Non-public technical information disclosed
   by the Owner remains confidential. Report vulnerabilities privately, as
   described in SECURITY.md or to contact@blueseatra.com. Do not exploit or
   disclose them before they are fixed.

8. Written permissions. Send requests to contact@blueseatra.com. A permission
   is valid only if it is written and signed by the Owner. It is personal,
   non-exclusive, non-transferable, and limited to its stated purpose, term
   and territory. Use of the Blueseatra online service is governed by its own
   terms, not by this licence.

9. No warranty and liability. To the extent permitted by law, the Software is
   provided "as is", without warranty of any kind. The Owner is not liable for
   damage caused by unauthorised use. This does not limit liability for gross
   negligence or wilful misconduct, or any liability that cannot be excluded
   by law.

10. Sanctions. Unauthorised use is infringement (French IP Code, art. L.335-2,
    L.335-3 and L.343-4) and may lead to civil and criminal proceedings and to
    claims for damages. Any permission granted ends automatically and without
    notice upon breach; all copies must then be destroyed.

11. Governing law and courts. French law applies. Subject to mandatory rules
    of jurisdiction, disputes fall under the competent courts within the
    jurisdiction of the Paris Court of Appeal. If a clause is held invalid,
    the others remain in force. Failure to exercise a right is not a waiver.

Contact: contact@blueseatra.com · https://blueseatra.com
